  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1114 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe main upper low and trough in the western U.S. will begin to \nswing through the area Wednesday which will lead to much higher \nchances of rain over the eastern half of the panhandle. At the same \ntime a cold front will be pushing down from the north and by evening \nshould be moving into the region. This will enhance showers and \nthunderstorms as there will be a general area of low pressure across \nsoutheast CO/southwest KS and other boundaries to provide focus \nfor storms. As the cold front moves through and winds become \nnortherly the precipitation should begin to move to the east and \nslowly out of the area. Even by Thursday morning there could still\nbe activity in the far southeastern portion of our area.\n\nDue to the clouds and precip Wednesday should only see high temps in \nthe 70s through the area. By Thursday high temperatures will be in \nthe upper 60s over the western third of the panhandle and by Friday \nhigh temps will likely be in the upper 50's to low 60's all areas. \nWill see low temps by Saturday morning in the mid to upper 30's \nover many areas and low 40's in the southeast.",
